    {
      "title": "Week 2 · Life on Mars",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "title": "Build the base",
          "goal": "Work out how the crew gets air and water, then design a greenhouse for food.",
          "modules": [
            {
              "id": "c-base",
              "kind": "content",
              "title": "Three things to stay alive",
              "minutes": 3,
              "body": "On Earth, air, water and food are easy. On Mars:\n\n- The **air** is thin and mostly carbon dioxide. We can't breathe it.\n- The **water** is frozen as ice, under the ground and at the poles.\n- **Food** has to be grown indoors, under lights, in a greenhouse.\n\nPass the base inspection, then design your greenhouse.",
              "attachments": [
                {
                  "kind": "image",
                  "url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Jezero_crater_on_Mars%2C_sol_43_of_Perseverance_mission.png/960px-Jezero_crater_on_Mars%2C_sol_43_of_Perseverance_mission.png",
                  "name": "Jezero crater, seen by the Perseverance rover",
                  "credit": "NASA / JPL-Caltech"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "g-inspect",
