              "id": "c-crumbs",
              "kind": "content",
              "title": "Why crumbs are a problem",
              "minutes": 2,
              "body": "In a spaceship, crumbs don't fall. They float into eyes, noses and machines! That's why astronauts eat tortillas instead of bread.",
              "attachments": [
                {
                  "kind": "image",
                  "url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/ISS-50_Peggy_Whitson_with_a_%27space_cheeseburger%27.jpg/960px-ISS-50_Peggy_Whitson_with_a_%27space_cheeseburger%27.jpg",
                  "name": "Astronaut Peggy Whitson with a “space cheeseburger”",
                  "credit": "NASA"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "a-snack",
              "kind": "answer",
              "title": "Invent a space snack",
              "minutes": 10,
              "body": "Invent a snack for the trip. Give it a name, say what's in it, and how it stays crumb-free. A drawing or a recording is welcome."
